* is the merchandise ordered quantity minus the quantity shipped. It is 0 when the order is complete or canceled. Freight and surcharge are left out. On a merchandise row, shipped of ordered sits after the line status, as `0 of 14`. **Print** on Order details opens **customer-order-print** in a new tab, with no app header and no menu. Shipping a customer shipment adds to `qty_shipped`.

## Customer shipments

Goods we ship to a **customer**. One shipment is one customer and can carry **several orders**, as long as their ship-to, bill-to, terms, shipping method, and sales rep are the same (migration 0069). Staff page `/customer-shipments`. Admin and warehouse write. A sales rep only reads the shipments of customers that rep services.

1. `customer_shipments` — `shipment_no` (serial), `customer_id`, `status`, and a header copied from the **first order added**: ship-to and bill-to address columns (no address ids), `terms`, `shipment_method_id` and `shipping_method`, `sales_rep_id`. Also `created_at` (Date created), `date_shipped`, `picker_id` (a staff login), `created_by`, `updated_by`, `tracking_no`, `notes`, and `sage_invoice_no` (nullable text, the invoice number in Sage; a blank is stored as null; migration 0071). Status is pending, picking, picked, boxed & ready (`boxed_ready`), shipped, canceled. The header does not change while the shipment has order lines.
2. `customer_shipment_products` — `customer_order_id` + `product_id` (must be on that order), unique per shipment. No status. A freight or surcharge line may have no order (`customer_order_id` null). `qty` and `price` are used by charge lines only.
3. `customer_shipment_cells` — size/drop `qty` and `price`. The price is the **full unit price** (order line price plus the size extra), copied from the order when the line is added. Later order price edits do not rewrite the shipment.

**Add order** (`add_order_to_customer_shipment`) puts every open product of an approved, picking, or back-order order on the shipment, or only the products in its optional list (`p_product_ids`, migration 0074), with quantities set to what is left to ship (ordered minus shipped minus other open shipments). An order's charge is added once across its shipments. Quantities can be lowered, and cannot exceed what is left. An order with a line on an open shipment reads picking (see **Customer orders**).

The open statuses move freely in either direction. **Canceled** is final and writes nothing to stock or shipped quantities; its orders leave picking. **Ship** (`ship_customer_shipment`) is one all-or-nothing step from any open status: it refuses when a cell exceeds what is left on its order or what is on hand, then takes the stock off `inventory`, writes `stock_movements`, adds to `customer_order_cells.qty_shipped`, sets `date_shipped`, and locks the shipment. An order line that is fully shipped becomes complete, and the rollup then moves the order header. A short line is left for staff to mark back order or short shipped. No un-ship unless asked. After Shipped only the tracking number, the notes, and the Sage invoice number change. An order or an order product that is on a shipment cannot be deleted.

The page is fit-list+details, the same two panes as customer orders. **Add new shipment** sits above the list for admin and warehouse and opens a card with a Customer Combo Box. **Save** and **Cancel** appear after a customer is picked. **Save** creates the shipment and selects it. The list columns are Shipment, Date, Customer, Orders, Status, and Shipped. List rows have no buttons; the shipment number stays a link to the shipment page. Nothing selected reads **Select a shipment.** The details header is the customer name and **Shipment No {n}**, with the folder. For admin and warehouse, **Ship** sits there while the shipment is open and opens a card with **Date shipped** (today). **Ship** on that card ships it, with **Working…** beside it, and **Cancel** leaves it. After a thin divider, **Edit** and **Delete** sit in the `RowButtons` chip. **Delete** shows until the shipment is shipped, asks first, and removes the shipment with its lines; the orders are left as they were, apart from leaving picking when this was their last open shipment. A shipped shipment shows **Edit** only. A canceled shipment shows **Delete** only. **Edit** opens a card: Status (the open statuses and Canceled) and Picker (a Combo Box of admin and warehouse logins) while the shipment is open, then Tracking No, Sage invoice No, and Notes. A shipped shipment edits only Tracking No, Sage invoice No, and Notes. Saving Canceled asks first. **Save** and **Cancel** appear only after a field changes. Under the header: Picker, Tracking No, Sage invoice No, and Last updated by with no group title, then **Customer** (account, Sage, sales rep, entered by), **Terms and shipping** (terms, shipping method), **Ship to** and **Bill to**, Notes, and a pinned **Shipment summary**: one row per item, **Total quantity**, **Surcharges**, **Freight**, and **Grand total**, for the quantities on this shipment (`summarizeOrder`). Clicking it or the folder opens a right dock of the products, 95% wide, titled the customer name and **Shipment No {n}**. For admin and warehouse while the shipment is open, **Add to shipment** is a centered bar with **Order** and **Charges**. **Order** opens a Combo of that customer's approved, picking, and back-order orders. Picking an order widens the popup and lists the products Add order can still put on this shipment (`loadAddableOrderProducts`), in the Fit List look: a checkbox, the product name, and **To add** (the left-to-ship units, or a charge's amount). Every row starts checked, and a header checkbox checks or unchecks all. Clicking a row toggles it. **Add** runs Add order for the checked products only, and with none checked reads **Check at least one product.** An order with nothing addable reads **Nothing is left to ship on this order.** and has no **Add**. **Charges** opens a Combo of active freight and surcharge that are not already on the shipment. The lines are a Fit List sorted by order number, product type, then name. Each row shows the product name and **Order No {n}** (or **No order**), then the size/drop matrix of the cells that were left to ship, then the extended amount: quantity times the cell's full unit price. Double-click the matrix to edit the quantities. A drop row taken off the grid is saved as 0. **Delete** removes the line from the shipment. A charge row shows the blue freight or blue surcharge image, with the cost or the quantity and price. Under the list: Freight, Surcharge, Merchandise, and Total. There is no line status, no price card, no Inventory, and no Copy. A shipped or canceled shipment, and a sales rep, see the rows read-only. Lowering a quantity is always allowed; raising one is refused above what is left. `/customer-shipments?shipment={id}` opens the page with that shipment selected.

## Pick list

A staff login's own list of order products to ship, like a cart. Admin and warehouse only. Page `/pick-list`, in the menu with a count of the picked products.

It is kept in the browser (`localStorage`, keyed by the login) until **Sign out** or **Clear**. Not a table. It holds ids only, as customer → that customer's orders → each order's picked products (`src/lib/pick-list.ts`, `usePickList`). No quantities are stored. The page reads the orders as they are now (`loadPickOrders`).

**Left to ship** here is `customer_order_cells.qty − qty_shipped` per size/drop cell, never below zero. Quantities on another shipment that has not shipped are not subtracted. A freight or surcharge line counts as left while it is on no shipment that is not canceled.

On Customer orders, **Pick** shows on a product row while the order is approved, picking, or back order, the line is pending or back order, something is left to ship, and the line is not on a shipment that has not shipped. A picked row reads **Picked**, and a second click takes it off. A line that is on a shipment that is not shipped and not canceled has no **Pick**. That spot reads **Picking** in yellow (`text-yellow-600`), plain text with no underline, for merchandise and charge rows and for every staff role. The stored line status under the product name is left as it is. **Pick** comes back when that shipment is shipped, canceled, or deleted, or the line is taken off it, while something is still left. **Pick all** in the Order details header adds every line that still shows **Pick**, reads **Picked** when they all are, and is hidden when there is none.

The page is fit-list+details. The left Fit List has one row per **branch**: one customer and one set of main properties (ship-to, bill-to, terms, shipping method, sales rep, `orderShipKey`), so a customer with two ship-to addresses has two rows. Columns are Customer, Ship to, Orders, and Products. The right side shows the selected branch: the customer name and product count, **Create shipment**, and **Remove** in the chip; then terms, shipping method, and sales rep, Ship to and Bill to, and a Fit List of each picked order followed by its picked products, with the left-to-ship quantity and a **×** on each order and each product. A line that can no longer ship shows the reason in red: the order is no longer approved, the line is no longer open, nothing is left to ship, or the line is already on a shipment (merchandise or a charge on a shipment that has not shipped, and a charge on a shipped one too). **Create shipment** reads **Take the red lines off first.** while a red line is on the branch. An order that was deleted, or a product taken off its order, leaves the list by itself. **Back** and **Clear** sit on the title row. **Back** opens Customer orders with that order's products panel open and the product selected (`/customer-orders?order={id}&product={id}`): the selected line, or else the product picked last. **Clear** asks first and empties the list. **Remove** asks first and takes the branch off.

**Create shipment** (`create_customer_shipment_from_picks`, migration 0070) creates one pending shipment for the branch with only the picked products, all or nothing. The first order fills the shipment header. Merchandise cells get what is left to ship at the full unit price, and a cell with nothing left is left off. It refuses, naming the line, when an order can no longer ship, the orders do not share the main properties, a line is no longer open, nothing is left, a line is already on a shipment that has not shipped (migration 0073), or a charge is already on a shipment. The branch then leaves the pick list, and the page links to the new shipment. The orders on it turn to picking. Nothing here ships: **Ship** on the shipment still does that.
